David Ernst

Usage:
    ingest-books [options] <inputDir> <outputDir>
Options:
    -h, --help
          Print this help page.
    -d, --discard-extras
          Discard what only costs bytes: drop the embedded fonts, delete the
          junk/teaser images, downscale the illustrations to at most fullHD,
          and strip a PDF's images. Off by default - none of it can be got
          back from the output.
    -c, --clean-structure
          Run clean-folder-structure on the output folder when done.
    -k, --keep
          Keep: an epub is copied across as a PDF is, rather than re-converted.
          The other formats are still converted to epub, once, without that
          re-conversion.
    -t, --text
          Text mode: convert every recognized input to a raw .txt file,
          mirroring the input sub-folder layout, instead of the epub pipeline.
    -z, --zpaq
          Text mode only: also create a zpaq archive of the resulting folder
          (output folder, or input folder when no conversion was done).
    -A, --ai
          Let language models help (docs/models.md). Without -A no step asks
          one; the commands this one starts are handed it.
    -v, --verbose
          Also say why each item was handled the way it was, and on a failure
          print the tool's whole output rather than its last lines.
    -q, --quiet
          Print errors only - no progress and no warnings.
    -x, --set <name=value>
          Override a setting for this run, over the settings file; repeatable. A
          secret is refused - the settings file is where it goes. The settings
          page lists the names.
